USB MIDI host: the USB-C port as the host of a class compliant USB-MIDI controller, alone or behind a powered hub
(chip/usb_host.c, chip/usb_host_desc.h; fm1_usb_host_attach and fm1_usb_line in chip/fm1_usb.h; usb.c: usb_poll
serves the host's IN endpoint, usb_retry leaves a host port alone, usb_detach ends it). Built only with
FELUCCA_USB_HOST 1 (fm1-base's FM1B_USB_HOST: patches/fm1-base/0002-usb-host.patch); the update loader never has it.
Each packet from the controller also goes to the MIDI tap (FM1B_MIDI_TAP, 0001), SysEx too.
Why MIDIMON needs it: to monitor (and pass on with THRU) a USB-MIDI controller plugged into the FM-1 itself.

Origin and licence: Melodee pull request #75 by Adrien Tibi (Recursive Field Instruments),
https://github.com/keremimo/melodee/pull/75 (commit 198c8fd), GPL-3.0-only in Melodee. Its author licensed his
code in it under MPL-2.0, in that pull request; the question and the answer, verbatim:
  keremimo, 2026-10-24, https://github.com/keremimo/melodee/pull/75#issuecomment-6383989315
    "Are you okay with licencing your part of the code as MPL? That would enable me to get this code into the
     fm1_base and also Saadet as well."
  recursivefieldinstruments, 2026-10-24, https://github.com/keremimo/melodee/pull/75#issuecomment-6384184014
    "Hey! Excellent. It works super well here. I've been using various controllers and that's so convenient.
     For the licensing, of course, feel free to do so :)
     Kind regards,
     Adrien Tibi (Recursive Field Instruments)"
This permission is the only ground for these files being MPL-2.0; a build with Bluetooth links JieLi's binary
libraries, so no GPL code may be in it (LICENSING.md). The register sequences are the AC79 SDK's (Apache-2.0).
Fitted to felucca-bsp by ignis32: FELUCCA_USB_HOST, felucca-bsp's USB audio state, usb_start on the way back, the
tap, uh_event for the platform. MIDI out to the controller (added in Melodee 1.5 RC by keremimo) is not here: that
is keremimo's code, under its own licence.
Applies to: felucca-bsp d6b8f77 (fm1-base aa2b3bc). Upstream: keremimo means to bring it to fm1-base (same thread).
